# Profile organisation-0.1 (Core 0.4 Stage D-2, LABS-1.026). Additive vocabulary only (D-D-1, D-D-9): installed after
# the full core with WorldModel.install_profile("organisation"). Membership (member-of), organisational structure
# (part-of), ordinary roles, abilities (capability classifications) and agency are core.
define
# sortals: a person and an organisation (or one of its units) have different identity criteria (v0.2 §3.1)
entity person sub physical-object;
entity organisation sub social-object;
# employment: a contingent social relation between an organisation and a person (v0.2 §3.4)
relation employment sub proposition, relates employer, relates employee;
organisation plays employment:employer;
person plays employment:employee;
# holding an office (a social-role concept) in a context (an organisation or unit). A subtype of classified-as, so
# generic role queries see it; no functional slot is declared: exclusivity is the attested constraint below, and
# nothing is ever inferred about people no appointment mentions (LABS-1.026)
relation office-holding sub classified-as;
# a single-holder constraint on one office within one context, attested over its own valid time (and disputable like
# any content). When it holds and several accepted appointments overlap, the reports say DISPUTED and cite both
relation exclusive-office sub proposition, relates office, relates context;
social-role plays exclusive-office:office;
particular plays exclusive-office:context;
# conferred authority: who (grantor) conferred which power (a capability concept) on whom (holder) within what
# (scope). The reporting source is the attestation's attester, independent of the grantor. It establishes nothing
# about the grantor's own entitlement (D-D-3); there are no delegation chains
relation authorisation sub proposition, relates grantor, relates holder, relates power, relates scope;
particular plays authorisation:grantor, plays authorisation:holder, plays authorisation:scope;
capability plays authorisation:power;
# an act undertaken in an office: the official (as actor; one specialisation, D-D-6), the office and its context.
# An account of it establishes neither its occurrence, nor the office, nor any authority
relation official-act sub event, relates official as actor, relates office, relates office-context;
particular plays official-act:official;
social-role plays official-act:office;
particular plays official-act:office-context;
